  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write J6" at 01:58 CST 2026-11-24, re-cut on the J1 write, with no debate run live (Wall 11483; audit 41331). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 0714bdd9 to 04273989-a679-4315-9b40-c84d5260dbce; child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT be711308 to c9acb53a-ddcc-4ccc-9149-900f6e9e140a. Shared Library only, in each: library lines 3194, 3196, 3371, 3373 to 3376 and 3496. LIB 3e42df7e04db6ad2, MAP 97ab265d3c9de960. This is the live engine at the draft of this row. THE FAULT IT ANSWERS (card586j6.md section 1): in run 42071 the enforcer told qwen4max that its break on D2 vs C6 was wrong, citing one verse (Luke 1:33); the judge's GROUND rested on Jeremiah 22:30 and Acts 2:30, which the enforcer never answered; that item began the seat's removal (debate_enforcer_log rows 53043, then 53144). What is live: (1) the enforcer's E-COL text gains: "A DISAGREE answers every verse on the judge's GROUND line: for each one, a clause that quotes it and says why it does not carry the judge's grade, or one CARRIED BY for each. A DISAGREE that leaves a verse of the GROUND unanswered is recorded and not sent back." (2) The E-HOLD text gains the same sentence with "says why it leaves the point open". (3) Code (gateJ6): before a DISAGREE goes to a judge, every verse on the judge's GROUND, read from the whole line, must be cited in the enforcer's answer to that item, and every CARRIED BY must pass the existing check, not only the last; an ENGAGE line answered NO is not an answer. A miss is held with the record "RECORDED, NOT SENT BACK, ASK 586 J6: the enforcer's DISAGREE does not answer <refs>, on the judge's GROUND". No seat, no count. (4) The reply parser keeps each item's following lines whole. LIVE, NOT A TRIAL (ruling row 512); the card said that this reverses the plan's earlier "TRIAL first". The path: W3's texts draft 2 (W1 PASS, Wall 11460, 11468); build rev 0 on d819ff4c (Wall 11472); W1 PASS (Wall 11474); the card; the press; the re-cut on the J1 write and the write (Wall 11483); W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11485). IN PART, for two reasons. (1) No run has executed on 04273989; the first live run is the first test of the new enforcer text. (2) THE WRITTEN TARGET IS A RE-CUT MADE AFTER THE GRADE. W1 graded the build on base d819ff4c (targets 0fa135d5 and 02af2f0b) and wrote "Re-cut on whichever of 595, J1 and J3 is written first" (Wall 11474). The re-cut on the J1 write (0da7d54f, f7b64378) was not graded before the write; W1's readback (Wall 11485) found 0 differences to j6recut and "The J1 to J6 change equals my own J6 change line for line, both before and after text", engine and child. LIMITS, as the card states them: a citation counts as an answer, the code does not read the clause's reasoning; a right correction by the enforcer that skips one verse of the GROUND no longer reaches the judge; a range needs a citation of the whole range; no run-wide count on 42071 can be given (its stored judge lines are cut at 1,500 and only 5 rows keep the whole reply). W1 did not trace the record path beyond the hold shape (Wall 11474). W4's mistake at this write, stated by W4 (Wall 11483): its check before the J6 write listed one running execution (42163) and the script did not stop on it; it was the workflow "TRUTH App -- Protected Table Snapshot to Drive", not the engine; W1 confirmed it was outside these flows (Wall 11485). W4's write scripts now refuse when any engine or child execution is running. RUN REVISION (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has executed or that a path is unexercised, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-42373-tg0w4edj (debate_results e7f6922f, row created 17:21 CST 2026-11-24; engine 20db58ee, child 74353c40; anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 as the Oracle defending against anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; outcome UNDERDETERMINED, panel BROKEN 2-1). The record-only side is shown: ten E-COL rows read "RECORDED, NOT SENT BACK, ASK 586 J6". The always line (a DISAGREE that answers every GROUND verse is sent back as before) was NOT shown for the panel, because no panel send-back was sent in this run; that is the ASK 611 defect and not a finding against J6. In this run no panel send-back was sent (53 of 58 rows read "NOT SENT: no panel request for this seat"; the cause is the ASK 611 build, since fixed by fix 2 and not shown by a run), so nothing that needs a panel send-back was shown. The operator's rule of 10:38 CST 2026-11-24 asks two live runs with no issues; status stays 'read back'.$t$,
